<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela's Lagoven doubles gasoline exports.</title>
<headline>Venezuela's Lagoven doubles gasoline exports.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lagoven, a subsidiary of state-owned Petroleos de Venezuela, sold 53,700 barrels per day (bpd) of gasoline on international markets in 1996, more than two times the volume sold in 1995, the company said in a press statement Tuesday.</p>
<p>Of the 53,700 bpd, 33,500 bpd was reformulated gasoline, used principally in the United States.</p>
<p>Lagoven said 1996 saw its first gasoline exports to Mexico and the company signed a contract to supply 3,600 bpd to that country in 1997.</p>
<p>((-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
